A15. Born. ~ NEE
A16. Puts a sofa and a girl to practical use. ~ NESTLES
A18. The devil you say? You're right. ~ LUCIFER
A20. A rubberless check. ~ TAB
A21. A true-blue cloud sweeper-away. ~ PAL
A23. The beginning of a spring song. ~ TRA
A24. Here's a weather-beaten lot for you, tho they do have a lot of pull at college. ~ CREW
A26. That's all there is—there isn't any more. ~ FINIS
A28. Add a sack to this and you'll have a neat little load. ~ KNAP
A30. This is almost a sneeze. ~ KER
A31. These have a way of pending. ~ PATENTS
A33. The loudspeaker his wife wrapped around his neck. ~ TIE
A34. Ockey doakey. ~ YES
A35. Careful, too much of this'll give you a sore head. ~ IRE
A36. Spanish saxophones. ~ GUITARS
